    <p><strong>Perfect for:</strong> Audiophiles with USB DACs, vinyl archivists, classical collectors, and anyone who wants their library with them outside the house.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

      <p><strong>What stays free?</strong></p>
      <p>Everything you need to run Orbit at home: the server, the apps, library import and management, and local playback on a single server.</p>

      <p><strong>How does the subscription work?</strong></p>
      <p>Orbit Pro is purchased through the App Store and managed from your Apple account. One subscription unlocks Pro on all your Apple devices, and you can cancel anytime.</p>

      <p><strong>What happens if I cancel?</strong></p>
      <p>Your library and all your data stay exactly where they are — on your server. Pro features lock back to the free tier; nothing is deleted.</p>

      <p><strong>Is there a free trial?</strong></p>
      <p>Yes. The annual plan starts with a 7-day free trial with all Pro features unlocked.</p>

      <p><strong>Do I need an internet connection?</strong></p>
      <p>No. Orbit runs entirely on your home network. Internet is only used for metadata lookups, and for remote listening through Orbit Cloud if you choose to enable it.</p>

      <p><strong>Can I use Orbit commercially?</strong></p>
      <p>Orbit is for personal, non-commercial use. Contact us for commercial licensing.</p>
    </section>

